    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_dab_builds_information_bottleneck_fr",
          "text": "DAB builds on the Information Bottleneck framework but replaces its rate term with an achievable rate borrowed from rate-distortion theory with finite cardinality.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "dab",
            "builds",
            "information",
            "bottleneck",
            "framework",
            "but",
            "replaces",
            "its",
            "rate",
            "term"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_concretely_learns_codebook_centroid",
          "text": "Concretely, the model learns a codebook of centroid distributions that quantize the encoders of all training points. The uncertainty of a new example is simply its expected statistical distance, here the Kullback-Leibler divergence, from that codebook.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "concretely",
            "learns",
            "codebook",
            "centroid",
            "distributions",
            "quantize",
            "encoders",
            "all",
            "points",
            "uncertainty"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_alternates_between_gradient_updates",
          "text": "Training alternates between gradient updates of the encoder and decoder and cheap analytic updates of the soft assignments and centroids, echoing the classic Blahut-Arimoto algorithm.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "alternates",
            "between",
            "gradient",
            "updates",
            "encoder",
            "decoder",
            "cheap",
            "analytic",
            "updates",
            "soft"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c4_result_closely_analogous_gaussian_pr",
          "text": "The result is closely analogous to a Gaussian Process, where the codebook plays the role of inducing points and statistical distance replaces Euclidean distance.",
          "expected_role": "result",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "result",
            "closely",
            "analogous",
            "gaussian",
