          "anchor_id": "cue_s10_c1_takeaway_recasting_uncertainty_probl",
          "text": "The takeaway is that recasting uncertainty as the problem of compressing training data into a learned codebook gives a single deterministic network a genuine sense of distance from what it has seen, letting it match or beat expensive ensembles at a fraction of the cost.",
